# Neo Learn Wavefolder parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.10). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnWavefolder
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnFold
class NeoLearnWavefolderMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching wavefolder: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A sine (with phase-locked FM from a second sine) pushed through one to six folding stages with a symmetry offset, then a low-pass gate that dims the brightness as the note fades and takes a strike at note-on, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for metallic basses, bongo-like plucks, sizzling leads and West Coast timbres, or to learn how wavefolding makes harmonics.

group Core
FoldDrive        "Wavefold" 0 1000 450 pct
    id fold_drive
    how Amplifies the pure sine/triangle oscillator past the folding threshold so wave peaks invert back into the waveform multiple times.
    sound Instead of clipping flat, the sound blooms with rich, metallic, and organic West Coast overtones.
FoldSymmetry     "Symmetry" 0 1000 500 bip
    id fold_symmetry
    how Injects a DC bias offset prior to the wavefolder so positive and negative halves of the wave fold unequally.
    sound Shifts the harmonic balance between hollow odd harmonics (centered) and warm, nasal even harmonics (offset).
FoldStages       "Fold Stages" 0 5 2 int 1
    id fold_stages
    how Selects how many series folding circuits the signal passes through.
    sound Lower stages sound warm and woody; 6 stages create dense, sizzling harmonic complexity on slight envelope sweeps.
TimbreFm         "Timbre FM" 0 1000 0 pct
    id linear_fm
    how Applies phase-locked audio-rate frequency modulation to the core oscillator before it hits the wavefolder.
    sound Causes the folded peaks to churn and intermodulate, producing complex percussive and aggressive textures.
LpgMode          "Low-Pass Gate" 0 1000 600 pct
    id lpg_mode
    how Morphs the output stage from a clean VCA (0%) to an optical low-pass gate (100%) that dims brightness as volume drops.
    sound Gives notes a natural, woody, acoustic bongo/marimba ring-out where high frequencies decay faster than bass.
GateStrike       "Gate Strike" 0 1000 300 pct
    id lpg_ping
    how Hits the virtual optical gate with a sharp transient impulse at note-on.
    sound Adds an organic, percussive "thwack" to the front of bass notes and West Coast plucks.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 150 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 520 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 600 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 450 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 590 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnWavefolderMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
